%% Sequence R3: wake-only push and seq-driven sync (from 0.5), including the OEM-throttling fallbacks.
%% ADRs: ADR-0019 (push is wake-only from 0.5), ADR-0014 (pull by seq, change feed), ADR-0013 (persist before ack),
%%       ADR-0012 (FcmHintSource / RestChangeFeedSource as InboundSources), ADR-0020 (DB key readable after first unlock).
%% Status: Proposed - pending owner approval in docs/architecture/multi-transport/APPROVAL.md. No code before approval.
%% Source of truth: decision brief ADR-0019, sections 6.4, 9 (wake-up); SAD section 6.3 (R3) step table.
%% Evidence: BE-15 (message content in FCM payload = KVKK Art. 9 transfer to a US processor), MOB-10 (background sync
%%   on device clock), MOB-11, R11 (OEM throttling). Residual (token + timing) with counsel: Q-L6(b), open item OI-42.
%% Rules:
%%   1. Payload is exactly {t: "wake", v: 1}, optionally a random per-device hint token mapped server-side:
%%      no content, no sender name, no preview, no conversationId, no seq (ADR-0019, resolved 2026-11-12).
%%   2. Notification text is composed on the device from the local DB; it never leaves the device.
%%   3. Any lost wake is repaired by the next pull (P6): foreground, reconnect, WorkManager / BGTask.
%%   4. Verification: captured FCM payload contains no content, conversation id or seq (RQ-07, 0.5 exit); owner observes a notification with
%%      the app killed (0.5 exit) and the message in the DB before the tap (0.6 exit).
sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    participant SM as SendMessageService
    participant HP as DeliveryHintPublisher
    participant HPort as DeliveryHintPort<br/>(WsAndFcmHintAdapter)
    participant WR as WsSessionRegistry
    participant WP as WakePushService<br/>(WakePushPort, FcmWakePush)
    participant FCM as FCM (APNs later)<br/>external processor
    participant FH as FcmHintSource<br/>(recipient app, killed or backgrounded)
    participant SC as SyncCoordinator
    participant RF as RestChangeFeedSource
    participant API as Backend /changes
    participant IB as Inbox + SQLCipher DB
    participant RS as ReceiptService
    participant NT as Local notification
    participant WM as WorkManager / BGTask

    SM-)HP: MessageAccepted(conversationId, seq) after commit
    HP->>HPort: hint(device, conversationId, seq) for every recipient device
    par WS hint to every live session
        HPort-)WR: sync.hint / message.new (see seq-send-receive)
    and wake to every recipient device, including the sender's own other devices
        HPort->>WP: wake(device, opaque hint token, collapseKey per device)
        WP->>FCM: high-priority data-only message {t: "wake", v: 1}
        FCM-)FH: deliver (best effort, may be delayed or dropped by OEM)
    end
    Note over HP,WP: presence-aware suppression for devices with a live WS session is a later refinement (brief section 4.2, ICD W-5)

    FH->>SC: wake (no conversation named)
    SC->>RF: heads() - lastSeq per conversation in one request (ICD 4.3)
    SC->>IB: watermark w per conversation
    alt some head > w
        SC->>RF: changes(conversationId, afterSeq = w, limit) for each advanced conversation
        RF->>API: GET /api/v1/conversations/{id}/changes?afterSeq&limit over TLS
        API-->>RF: {items, nextAfterSeq, lastSeq, hasMore}
        RF-->>SC: page
        SC->>IB: apply page
        IB->>IB: one tx per page - upsert items + w := nextAfterSeq (repeat while hasMore)<br/>C := lastSeq only when hasMore = false (ICD 3.8 R-ACK)
        IB->>RS: complete through C
        RS->>RS: queue CONTROL message.ack {conversationId, uptoSeq = C, DELIVERED} in the CONTROL lane<br/>(not an outbox_entry row; after commit, P4), sent when ServerLink or RestServerLink is Ready (spec 6.6, R-5)
        IB->>NT: compose notification text locally from DB rows
    else no head above w (duplicate or stale wake)
        SC->>SC: no-op
    end

    opt wake lost or throttled (R11 fallback)
        Note over FH,WM: Pull is truth - no message depends on the wake arriving
        WM->>SC: periodic sync, driven by server seq (not the device clock, MOB-10)
        SC->>RF: heads() - lastSeq per conversation in one request
        RF->>API: conversation list with lastSeq
        API-->>RF: heads
        SC->>RF: changes() for each stale conversation
        Note over SC: Also on app foreground and on WS reconnect (Syncing(heads)).<br/>Known aggressive OEMs get an in-app battery-optimisation exemption notice.
    end

    Note over FH,NT: iOS (when the iOS app exists) - Notification Service Extension performs the fetch,<br/>DB key in Keychain with AfterFirstUnlockThisDeviceOnly so background wake can read it
